V8 inspector: give error-stack inspection a microtasks scope.

The error-stack helper added by patches/1026 calls V8 property APIs.
With Blink's scoped microtasks policy those calls need a MicrotasksScope,
just as getErrorProperty already has. Without it a JavaScript exception
evaluated over CDP terminates the renderer in a DCHECK-enabled build and
leaves the host waiting for the evaluation callback. Suppress microtasks
while inspecting the stack, preserving the observer's existing behavior.

--- a/v8/src/inspector/value-mirror.cc
+++ b/v8/src/inspector/value-mirror.cc
@@ -320,6 +320,8 @@ v8::MaybeLocal<v8::Value> getErrorStack(v8::Local<v8::Context> context,
                                         v8::Local<v8::Object> object) {
   v8::Isolate* isolate = v8::Isolate::GetCurrent();
   v8::TryCatch tryCatch(isolate);
+  v8::MicrotasksScope microtasksScope(context,
+                                    v8::MicrotasksScope::kDoNotRunMicrotasks);
   v8::Local<v8::String> name = toV8String(isolate, "stack");
   v8::Local<v8::Value> descriptor;
   if (object->GetOwnPropertyDescriptor(context, name).ToLocal(&descriptor) &&
